// In Lighthouse, excess_blob_gas is present in ExecutionPayloadDeneb/Electra/Fulu headers.
// beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs line 474: excess_blob_gas is passed in payload header.

// NOTE: gas_used <= gas_limit validation is primarily done by the EL.
// Lighthouse CL passes gas_used and gas_limit in payload header but does not independently enforce this.
// The EL validates gas_used <= gas_limit in validate_header.
// beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs line 429 (approx): gas_used, gas_limit in header.
// If EL rejects due to gas_used > gas_limit, it returns INVALID status to CL.

// NOTE: SYSTEM_ADDRESS (0xfffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffe) is an EL concept.
// Lighthouse CL does not set system transaction origin; this is done by the EL internally.
// The EL's process_system_transaction always sets caller/origin to SYSTEM_ADDRESS.
// Lighthouse path: beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs -> engine_newPayloadVX
// CL only passes execution requests; EL handles system transaction caller assignment.

// NOTE: calculate_base_fee_per_gas is an EL responsibility (EIP-1559 fee market).
// Lighthouse CL stores base_fee_per_gas from execution payload header but does not compute it.
// EL spec formula:
//   if gas_used > gas_target:
//     base_fee_delta = max(base_fee * (gas_used - gas_target) / gas_target / BASE_FEE_MAX_CHANGE_DENOMINATOR, 1)
//     new_base_fee = base_fee + base_fee_delta
//   else:
//     base_fee_delta = base_fee * (gas_target - gas_used) / gas_target / BASE_FEE_MAX_CHANGE_DENOMINATOR
//     new_base_fee = base_fee - base_fee_delta
// beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs: base_fee_per_gas in header (line ~429)

// NOTE: EL transaction validation ordering is an EL responsibility.
// Lighthouse CL does not implement transaction_validation_dispatch.
// In Lighthouse, P2P gossip validation occurs at the beacon block level (not EL transaction level).
// Relevant CL check ordering in beacon_node/network/src/network_beacon_processor/gossip_methods.rs:
// process_gossip_block -> process_gossip_unverified_block -> verify_block_for_gossip
// CL checks order: slot validity -> proposer index -> signature -> execution payload
// EL checks order (in EL codebase): type -> fees -> nonce -> balance -> blob-specific -> authorization

// NOTE: extra_data <= 32 bytes validation is an EL responsibility.
// In Lighthouse CL, extra_data is present in ExecutionPayload as a variable-length byte vector.
// The max size is enforced by SSZ: extra_data field is bounded by MAX_EXTRA_DATA_BYTES = 32.
// beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs contains JsonExecutionPayload which passes extra_data.
// The EL's validate_header checks len(extra_data) <= MAX_EXTRA_DATA_BYTES.
// SSZ deserialization in Lighthouse would also reject payloads with extra_data > 32 bytes.

// NOTE: check_gas_limit (parent_gas_limit // 1024 bound) is an EL responsibility.
// Lighthouse CL stores gas_limit from execution payload but does not validate rate of change.
// EL spec check_gas_limit:
//   abs(gas_limit - parent_gas_limit) < parent_gas_limit // 1024
//   gas_limit >= GAS_LIMIT_MINIMUM
// Lighthouse path: beacon_node/execution_layer/src/engine_api.rs -> engine_newPayloadVX
// EL returns INVALID if gas_limit change exceeds bound.

